{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Gm]Before the larks were singing, before the ket[Eb]tle's call
The light [Gm]came over the mountain and spilled across [Bb]the wall
No word [Eb]was ever spoken, no voice was ev[Gm]er heard
But all [F]the sky was preaching and every cloud [Gm]a word
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The heavens [Eb]declare the glory [Bb]of God
The skies [F]proclaim the work of [Gm]his hands
Day af[Eb]ter day they pour [Bb]forth speech
Night af[F]ter night they reveal knowl[Gm]edge
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The sun [Gm]comes like a bridegroom, rejoicing in his [Eb]strength
He runs from [Gm]end to end of heaven the whole of the day's [Bb]length
And nothing hides [Eb]from his warming, no valley and no [Gm]stone
And [F]so the word of the LORD goes out to make his goodness [Gm]known
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The heavens de[Eb]clare the glory of [Bb]God
The skies pro[F]claim the work of his [Gm]hands
Day after [Eb]day they pour forth [Bb]speech
Night after [F]night they reveal knowl[Gm]edge
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
